    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1351-26": {
      "title": "Senior Leisure Assistant ( Internal Only )",
      "description": "1351-26 Senior Leisure Assistant ( Internal Only ) - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Senior Leisure Assistant ( Internal Only ) Campus Services Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £27,319 to £29,588\r\n            per annum Grade: Grade 06 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 26 October 2026 Interview Date: To be confirmed Reference: 1351-26 Release Date: Monday 12 October 2026 Expression of Interest: Senior Leisure Assistant Woodcock Sports Centre, Aston University We invite staff to submit an expression of interest for the Senior Leisure Assistant role at Woodcock Sports Centre, Aston University. The successful applicant will play a key role in supporting the effective day-to-day operation of the Sports Centre, upholding high standards of customer service, health and safety, and operational compliance. Responsibilities will include supervising swimming pool activities, overseeing the management and maintenance of the plant room in accordance with operational and safety procedures, and ensuring that leisure assistants, gym instructors and external instructors adhere to departmental operational procedures. The postholder will also act as the designated person in charge during incidents, ensuring that all matters are managed promptly, appropriately and in line with the department’s Emergency Action Plan procedures. Anyone interested in applying for this opportunity must submit a written expression of interest by 2 6 th October 2026. Your written application should briefly outline your suitability for the role, relevant experience, and the skills and qualities you would bring to the position. This role does not meet the eligibility criteria for new applicants to the Skilled Worker visa route. See here for information about Skilled Worker eligibility criteria: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Thank you for your interest. Michele Robins Facilities Operations Manager Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Senior Leisure Assistant ( Internal Only ) Research Associate in Mathematics Postdoctoral Research Associate - Membrane Protein Folding View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
